# Kanban bug cards

When a feature file has frontmatter `labels: ["bug"]`, follow [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Bug cards.

## Frontmatter (agent creates)

```yaml
labels: ["bug"]
```

Use the **inline JSON array** form exactly — not a YAML block list (`labels:\n  - bug`).

## User provides

- `## Steps to Reproduce`
- `## Current Behavior` (legacy: `## What happens`)
- `## Expected Behavior`
- `## Feature Areas`
- `## QA Review` (during Review, if follow-up issues found)

## Agent provides (pre-implementation card review, before `in-progress`)

- `## Root Cause (current code)` — after reading Product scope + codebase
- `## Acceptance Criteria` — behavior-only fix bullets
- `## Out of Scope` — optional
- `## Product Paths` — resolved from Feature Areas via `docs/feature-areas.yaml` (no `tests/`)
- `## Product Methods` — symbols to edit (when Feature Areas set)
- `## Tests` — **Files**, **Methods**, **Verify (agent)**
- `## Docs` — doc paths + § hints
- `## Corrective Action` — concrete fix plan (**not** `## Decisions`); append **`**QA follow-up (YYYY-MM-DD):**`** bullets when fixing Review issues (§ User-reported QA fixes)

**Legacy alias:** `done/` / `archived/` cards may use **Label Paths** / **Label Methods** — parsers read
as Product (Signature: `kanban-card-scope-schema`).

## User-reported QA fixes

When fixing **Review** issues the user reports (chat, screenshots, or **`## QA Review`**):

1. Implement the fix; run targeted pytest when code changes.
2. **Append** a dated `**QA follow-up (YYYY-MM-DD):**` bullet under **`## Corrective Action`** — symptom, fix, test/doc pointer; add **`Scope:`** note when Product/Tests/Docs were appended.
3. **Refresh scope on the card** (same turn, when code changed):
   - **`## Feature Areas`** — append area label if fix crossed into a new product area.
   - **`## Product Paths`** — append any edited/added product paths not already listed.
   - **`## Product Methods`** — append symbols touched.
   - **`## Tests`** — append test files / `test_*` methods.
   - **`## Docs`** — append doc paths when user-visible docs changed.
   - **`docs/feature-areas.yaml`** — when new paths/handlers are durable for that area.
4. Bump `modified`. Optionally mark matching **`## QA Review`** `[x]`.

**Do not** skip the card update — the card is the audit trail. Full workflow: kanban-markdown § User-reported QA fixes.

## Card Done — lessons learned

When the user signals **QA-complete / Done** on a bug card, the **agent** moves to `done/` and
runs Card Done **same turn** (Signature: `card-done-agent-move-qa-complete`):

1. Read all **Corrective Action** + **QA follow-up** bullets on the card.
2. Capture durable lessons in **≥1 area skill** + **≥1 scoped rule** + **`docs/`** (and `feature-areas.yaml` / `registries/` when applicable).
3. Add **`## Lessons captured (YYYY-MM-DD)`** on the card with links to updated artifacts.
4. Add **`## Forward-looking feedback (YYYY-MM-DD)`** after Lessons captured (Signature:
   `card-done-forward-feedback` — [reference.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md)
   § Forward-looking feedback: Impact Scope, References, Mitigation on max tier, Importance
   when tied; top-3 in chat on Card Done turn).

Full checklist: kanban-markdown § Card Done — lessons learned capture.

## Do not

- Use `## Decisions` on bug cards — use `## Corrective Action`
- Start implementation with empty or disputed **Corrective Action**
- Move to **Review** without all **Acceptance Criteria** marked `[x]`
- Put method names only in **Product Paths** — use **Product Methods** (files-only paths in Product Paths; tests in **Tests**)
- Treat **deferred scope** on a parent feature card (documented Out of Scope) as a bug — spawn a **feature** card instead unless behavior contradicts shipped AC
- **Properties inspector / Save Layer** — variant, material, or direction changes with a selected cell but no dirty flag → `brush_inspector_changed` + `_apply_inspector_to_selected_cell`; Signature: `properties-inspector-live-apply` ([ui-change/SKILL.md](../skills/ui-change/SKILL.md) § Properties brush — live apply)

## Spawn from parent QA Review

When the user asks to record QA findings as bug cards (not fix in place on the parent):

- Parent feature card: **`## QA Review`** + **`## Spawned bug cards`** table; note failed **Verify** lines when applicable
- Child cards: `labels: ["bug"]`, `status: "todo"`, same `epic` as parent when part of a series
- Set **`order`** (`a0`, `a1`, …) in **implementation sequence** on the parent **`## Spawned bug cards`** table
- Lanterns / attachables explicitly deferred in parent **Out of Scope** → document in QA as deferred, not a bug card
- Orbit **bed merged pair** QA (foot top bake on head half) → epic `OrbitFunctionalFaceTextures`
  **a1** — split mattress top quads by head/foot part; not a0 color lookup alone.
- Orbit preview bugs that mismatch 2D facing — reuse existing 2D rotation helpers (`corner_stair_facing_rotation`, `normalize_direction`) in 3D box builders; **mirror south-authored boxes on local Z** before rotation so `@south` treads sit on +Z (matches `build_stair_top_mask` / `test_paste_corner_stair_matches_worldgen_facing`). **2D straight stairs:** `_prepare_topdown_texture` must use `stairs_behavior` + `corner_stair_facing_rotation` — not `rotate_directional_texture` (Signature: `2d-stair-facing-rotation`). **QA slab-like Top Down after facing fix** → spawn **feature** card for bake-time riser ghost fill — not a direction bug.
- Orbit stair **holes / transparency** (Signature: `orbit-stair-mask-transparency`) — **check textures before geometry**: 2D L-mask bakes on 3D faces + alpha discard look like missing mesh; fix with **full solid tiles** in `resolve_orbit_face_texture` (`PLANKS:{material}` for plank materials; `minecraft:{material}` for stone — not `PLANKS:cobblestone`), corner-probe `box_face_occluded` on `±Y`, riser box, same-cell culling; **do not** void-fill with masked tiles. QA: `structures/test/stage1`, `residence/stage1`, `well/stage1` cobblestone stairs. Tests: `test_orbit_stair_face_textures_are_opaque`, `test_orbit_cobblestone_stair_face_textures_are_opaque`, `test_lower_stair_slab_top_face_visible_on_open_half`
- Orbit **fence / wall black rail gaps** (Signature: `orbit-fence-mask-transparency`) — **not** solid tiles on post faces (fills gaps with wood). Keep **masked** `FENCE:*` / `WALL:*` bakes on thin box geometry; shader **`if (sample.a < 0.05) discard`** (stairs/slabs use opaque tiles — safe). Tests: `test_orbit_fence_side_texture_uses_masked_bake`, `test_orbit_wall_side_texture_uses_masked_bake`

